# Blog categories ≠ recipe categories

Blog posts and recipes use **different** category systems. Never mix them.

| Domain | Table | TypeScript | Query helper |
|--------|-------|------------|--------------|
| Recipes | `public.categories` | `Category` | `getCategories()` |
| Blog posts | `public.blog_categories` | `BlogCategory` | `getBlogCategories()` |

Posts store selected blog category **ids** on `posts.categories` (`text[]`). That array must only reference `blog_categories.id` — never recipe category ids.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — recipe categories on a post form / save path
const cats = await getCategories();
await supabase.from("posts").update({ category_id: cats[0].id });

// ✅ GOOD
const cats = await getBlogCategories();
await supabase.from("posts").update({ categories: selectedBlogCategoryIds });
```

When adding category UI or admin tools for the blog, use `blog_categories` / `BlogCategory` / `getBlogCategories()`. Recipe category admin (`/admin/categories`) must not manage blog categories. Blog category admin lives at `/admin/blog-categories`.
